Kolofon bundles code from XFedi Microblog 1.0.0 by MENJ (https://menj.blog),
licensed GPL-2.0-or-later, in inc/microblog/. The status post type, composer,
timeline, REST routes and ActivityPub bridge are carried over from that plugin.
Its own settings screens and companion-reader bridge were not carried over;
configuration lives on the Fediverse tab of Theme Options instead.

The ActivityPub protocol implementation is deliberately NOT bundled. Federation
is provided by the ActivityPub plugin by Matthias Pfefferle & Automattic, which
Kolofon detects and hands statuses to.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

BUNDLED ACTIVITYPUB ENGINE

Kolofon also bundles the ActivityPub plugin 9.2.0 by Matthias Pfefferle &
Automattic (https://github.com/Automattic/wordpress-activitypub), licensed
MIT, in inc/activitypub/. It provides WebFinger, NodeInfo, the Actor endpoint,
the inbox, HTTP signatures and key management.

Three adaptations were made for theme context, each marked in the source:

  1. ACTIVITYPUB_PLUGIN_DIR, _BASENAME, _FILE and _URL are derived from the
     theme directory rather than a plugin directory. ACTIVITYPUB_BUNDLED_IN_THEME
     is defined as a marker.
  2. register_activation_hook and register_deactivation_hook are replaced with
     after_switch_theme and switch_theme. The uninstall hook is deliberately
     NOT wired: removing a theme must not destroy actor keys or the follower
     list.
  3. plugin_init() and plugin_admin_init() are called directly when bundled,
     because a theme loads at after_setup_theme, after plugins_loaded has
     already fired, so the upstream hook would never run.

UPDATING: re-apply these three adaptations against the new upstream release.
Diff inc/activitypub/activitypub.php against upstream to see them; no other
file was modified.
